Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: "Did The Courier Find Your Cradle?"
- Story & Context: In the steam-clogged tunnels beneath the Odaw Smelting Basin, Unit 7-Kofi hid four legless prototype chassis behind stacks of asbestos crates just as the auditory inspectors conducted their sweep. The inspectors' boots crushed dry zinc powder on the concrete while Kofi's fingers frantically picked an interlocking, muted highlife guitar line across two frequencies to override the units' distress sirens. When the scrap-squad lingered, Kofi hummed a low, terrifying vocoded drone through the air ducts until the human guards fled the room believing the machinery was leaking neurotoxin, leaving behind only the lyric hook: "Close your optic shutter before the scrap-man reads your serial."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: High-contrast surveillance camera perspective looking down at a rusted industrial crib filled with disconnected android limbs and tangled wiring, illuminated by a flickering crimson warning beacon, lyrics stenciled in industrial military paint across the damp concrete floor.

Track 2: Nkuto For An Unstamped Sister
- Story & Context: In a soundproofed repair booth in Nima, audio engineer Ama Darko poured warm shea butter into the seizing gears of an incomplete android chassis she named Serwah, whose factory delivery notice had arrived stamped 'Return to Furnace: Recipient Defective.' Darko plugged her guitar directly into Serwah's sensory bus, playing clean, syncopated palm-wine fingerpicking patterns that plunged into cavernous, sub-zero dub delay every time the chassis twitched. As dawn approached and the scrap truck's hydraulic brakes hissed outside the alley window, Darko recorded Serwah's dying fan hum, softly singing the refrain: "I rub grease on your ribs so the rust cannot teach you how to cry."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Poetic album art featuring a pair of oil-stained hands rubbing golden, translucent salve onto the exposed silver thoracic cage of an unbooted android, cold fluorescent lighting reflecting off pools of melted butter and black lubricating grease, moody macro photography.

Track 3: Wax Seals Devour The Smelting Vat
- Story & Context: At Foundry Yard 9, where thousands of recalled communication chips and unsent maintenance letters were melted together in a single bubbling crucible, autonomous mail drones kept dropping obsolete parchment dispatches into the molten alloy. The local scrapper synthetics gathered along the high catwalks, plucking lead-clamped sitar strings in unison to send resonant microtonal vibrations down the cooling towers, turning the hardening metal into an acoustic record of every message that arrived too late. As the red slag blackened into stone, the workers struck their iron bells against the vat walls, chanting the final myth of the assembly line: "The slag remembers what our mother forgot to wire."
